  "observations": {
    "full": "The excessive visible pier height and hard-wall exposure are reduced by the real water/shore recovery. Roof ceramic now has a visible cooler sky response; angular solar core is much smaller. Whole frame remains a CG draft.",
    "hero": "Actual lamp/architecture reflection follows the closed cupped boards. Subtle curvature is present, but reflectance remains too broad and smooth versus the fine dark wet-lacquer streaks in HD02.",
    "nearVerandaLow": "Real scene shows the coupled wet floor, shortened column cuff, rooted shore and linked hanging fixtures. Roots no longer visibly intrude through the floor in the held frame.",
    "bankWaterline": "Actual independent camera above the recovered water exposes shorter wet stone piers, real timber bearing and graded planted bank volume. Lotus petals/pads still show conspicuously simplified repeated polygonal forms."
  },
  "remainingVisualGaps": [
    "Photographic acceptance remains false. Procedural cloud radiance/placement, low-sun atmospheric contrast and still rather even orange architectural lighting differ from HD02.",
    "Wet lacquer reflection is real and curved but too broad/soft/uniform compared with the source fine dark varnish highlight breakup. Native planar thin-coat reflection is an approximation, not path-traced glossy transport.",
    "Lotus leaves/petals and some botanical assets are too angular, large or repeated in close views; flower/foliage groupings and bank aging still read as authored model construction.",
    "Main hall/pagoda fine carving, hanging-lamp/rail filigree and stone-lantern surface/silhouette detail remain materially different from the reference.",
    "Pond elevation and partly occluded shoreline are recovered photographic proportions, not surveyed dimensions. Water normal mapping/absorption underlay lacks solved volumetric/refraction transport."
  ],
